-## Measured semantics — out of scope
+## Usage across tool rounds
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+Issue #93 chooses a single summed usage argument: it preserves the callback shape and serves turn-level billing without requiring consumers to aggregate provider calls. A per-round breakdown is rejected for this change because it adds public surface without being needed for that use case. The signature must name the argument `totalUsage` so its meaning is visible without reading the implementation. This changes the recorded cost of tool-heavy turns and requires a MINOR release and a consumer-facing changelog entry.
+
+## Measured semantics
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the sum of input, output, and total tokens across every provider call in that turn; rounds without usage contribute nothing, an entirely unreported turn receives `undefined`, and totals reset for the next turn, while a single provider call retains its original usage ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call per turn, counting only rounds that report usage](../../src/orchestration/usage.acceptance.test.ts#L33)).
